# Voice of Gudalur — petition site caching rules.
#
# Cloudflare Pages and Netlify both read this `_headers` file from the publish
# directory; other hosts ignore it.
#
# WHY index.html must never be cached hard: the page is shared by link over
# WhatsApp / Instagram, whose in-app browsers cache aggressively. If the HTML is
# cached, visitors keep seeing the stale page after a redeploy. Revalidate every
# time; the page is ~24 KB and brotli-compresses to ~6 KB.

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Explicit charset for HTML files — without this, Cloudflare/Netlify serve
# text/html without a charset directive, so browsers fall back to ISO-8859-1
# and the UTF-8 em-dashes, curly quotes and Tamil/Malayalam/Kannada glyphs
# turn into mojibake (e.g. " â€" " instead of " — ").
/*.html
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

/*.htm
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

# The hero film, its poster frame, the logo, the background song and the
# self-hosted font subsets. None of these are content-hashed, so keep the TTL
# short enough that a re-encoded asset is picked up within a day, with a long
# stale-while-revalidate tail so the swap never costs the visitor a wait.
/media/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

# The campaign song. The Content-Type is stated rather than assumed, for exactly
# the reason it is stated on /docs/* below: with X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
# in force, a host that answered an .m4a with application/octet-stream makes the
# browser download the file instead of playing it - and since the song starts
# on its own as soon as the page opens, that failure would land as a silent
# page rather than a wrong header.
/media/gudalur-new-path.m4a
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
  Content-Type: audio/mp4

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

# The two grievance record pages, and the shared first-party assets they and the
# homepage load. Same reasoning as /index.html applies: these pages are shared
# over WhatsApp and Instagram, whose in-app browsers cache HTML aggressively,
# and a stale copy of a grievance record is worse than a slow one. The assets
# are unhashed (no ?v= fingerprint), so they get an hour rather than a day.
/grievances/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400

# The three published PDFs (the government reply, our appeal, and the
# Gudalur Transformation Plan). Browsers hand these to the built-in PDF viewer
# rather than rendering them, so there is nothing here to cache aggressively;
# one day covers a corrected upload without making a reader wait on a re-upload.
#
# The Content-Type is stated rather than assumed. Each document is offered
# twice - "Read" opens it in the reader's own PDF viewer, "Download" saves it -
# and the two only differ by that: no `download` attribute on Read, one on
# Download. With `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` in force below, a host that
# answered with application/octet-stream would make the browser download the
# file instead of showing it, and Read would become a second Download button.
# Netlify and Cloudflare both resolve .pdf to application/pdf on their own;
# this line is what keeps that true on any host, and matches what the local
# preview server is told to send.
/docs/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
  Content-Type: application/pdf

# Baseline security headers. The page is first-party by design: no third-party
# script, no iframe, no remote font. It makes exactly one cross-origin request -
# the POST to the support Worker that mints the Support ID - so connect-src names
# that one origin and nothing else. The Worker replies with an
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin for https://voiceofgudalur.space only, so a page
# served from anywhere else is refused before a record can be written from it.
# The official follow-up routes (tel:1100, the CM Helpline mailbox, the
# Mudhalvarin Mugavari portal) are plain <a href> links, which CSP does not
# restrict, so form-action stays 'self' and frame and img stay closed. If an
# embed is ever added back, re-open frame-src (and img-src, for its thumbnail
# host) here at the same time.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
